roloman – binary (de)serialization lib for C data types

DISCLAIMER:
THIS IS A HOBBY PROJECT AND THUS NOT INTENDED FOR PRODUCTION USE.
IT IS INTENTIONALLY NOT THREAD SAFE.

- (de)serialize aka. (un)roll C data types into binary buffers
- rolled buffers can be transmitted over the wire or stored on disk for later retrieval
- possibly with compression

Message Layout:
36B	HEAD
<=2^32B	Body

Binary Format (byte-length, purpose):
04B	Magic Name "ROLO"
02B	SemVer Major
02B	SemVer Minor
02B	SemVer Patch
02B	Alignment Padding
16B	SHA256 Schema File Hash
04B	Compression Indicator (default 0 for none)
04B	Message Length in bytes (compressed if Compression Indicator is set)
[ Body ]

Body		:= Sequence of Entity
Entity		:= EntityHead .. EntityBody
EntityHead	:= ByteLength(4B) .. TypeIndicator
TypeIndicator 	:= ContainerType(4B) .. ElementType(4B)
EntityBody	:= Binary(ByteLength)

